SUMMARY:Art Closing: Linda Antoinette Nelson at Montclair Brewery
DESCRIPTION:Come out for one final look at the works of our artist-in-residence: Linda Antoinette Nelson!\nLinda Antoinette Nelson is a NJ native and multimedia artist and an active member of the African American Cultural Committee at the Montclair Art Museum. Her work ranges from vibrant acrylic paintings inspired by nature and everyday moments to symbolic mixed-media compositions that explore identity\, resilience\, and social awareness. Whether celebrating the beauty of a summer landscape or weaving together visual metaphors and portraiture\, her work invites viewers to pause\, reflect\, and find connection in the world around them. \nCourage may be the most important of all virtues\, because without it one cannot practice any other virtue with consistency. – Maya Angelou \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
